                    <occupation>Presbyterian minister</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Identification made through Norwich 
  connection: Houghton, who was trained at the Warrington dissenting academy, was one 
  of the ministers at the Octagon in Norwich. Two of the five contacts are in Norwich and as 
  the rest are not far apart, and mostly connected to the J Johnson circle  
  we have coded all five for this Houghton. 
  </p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="printedbook">C.B. Jewson, <title>The Jacobin City: A Portrait of Norwich in its Reaction to the French 
